# DTF tier manifest: scan-ingest-and-workspace
#   (artifact-keeper#4669, #4667, #4668; all shipped in 1.11.1)
# Profile-set: filesystem + upstreams.mock-osv (api.osv.dev resolves to the
# stdlib-python OSV mock of the osv-positional-findings tier; the oracle
# registers the advisories). Grype, bundled in the backend image, is the
# filesystem scanner for #4668; no scanner sidecar.
#
# THE BUGS (all RED on 1.11.0)
#   #4669  The dependency scanner only asked OSV about an artifact's DECLARED
#          dependencies. A leaf package with none (an npm tarball whose
#          package.json has no `dependencies`) sent the feed nothing and graded
#          `complete`, 0 findings, with `live:osv` provenance. Fixed: the
#          artifact's own pinned identity joins the batch once, and is kept
#          out of its own dependency inventory (scan_packages).
#   #4667  POST /api/v1/security/findings/external with a NUL byte in a string
#          field answered 500 DATABASE_ERROR, after the scan_results row had
#          already been committed `completed`: a clean-looking verdict with no
#          findings under it. Fixed: 400 VALIDATION_ERROR from the field
#          deserializer, and the scan row and findings in one transaction.
#   #4668  Trivy/Grype filesystem scans extracted into a directory named only
#          by the artifact id, so concurrent scans of one artifact deleted each
#          other's tree. On 1.11.0 the visible symptom is silent: the losing
#          scans complete with an EMPTY inventory (0 scan_packages rows) rather
#          than failing. Fixed: one workspace per job (<artifact_id>-<job>).
#
# THE GATES
#   (CONTROL) every image: a declared PyPI dependency is queried and reported
#     through the mock; a clean external submission is ingested as one
#     completed scan with its finding; a lone grype scan of the npm tarball
#     catalogs the package.
#   (FIX) #4669, #4667, #4668: RED on 1.11.0, GREEN on 1.11.1 and later.
#     #4668 fires 3 rounds of 3 simultaneous bypass_dedup scans; on 1.11.0
#     every round has exactly one survivor (6 of 9 scans empty, measured).
#
# NOT GATED: the Trivy filesystem and OpenSCAP workspaces (same fix, no sidecar
# here); #4669's "queried once even when the manifest also names it" (needs a
# package that depends on itself).
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: ~30 API calls plus scan polling.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-osv"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
